-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for the universal
-- property of the completion (DESIGN.md §4): Arrows, the additions to
-- Functor, FunctorCat, PrecomposeFF (Lemma A), Descent (Lemma B),
-- UniversalProperty (Theorem 4.4), CompletionUP (instance 4.5).
-- Kinds: the parts of an iso (arr, inv, Iso, isIso) and cmp; the notions
-- each step names (Comp/Square/Natural/Nat, Cond/Conds/T, Squares/Legs/
-- Compat/Cocone/X/Singl/PathSp/Sqs/Y, EssSurj, FullyFaithful, isEquiv,
-- isProp/isSet); "by definition" of a construction (functor, nat, idn,
-- comp, pre, lift, lifted, conj, t).  In Lemma B the descended functor's
-- objects and arrows are the centres of X_b and Y_g (obj, eta, map are
-- components of X-inh, Y-inh): unit, counit, iso and Pair.square open them.
